**Stack:** React · TypeScript · Vite · TanStack Query · React Hook Form · Zod ·
Tailwind CSS · SCSS Modules · ShadCN UI · Radix UI

## Lead Lens: foolproof audit gate

Design review challenges the **design**. The **Lead Lens** audits what was
**actually built**, with evidence, before anything is called done.

- **Gate mode (automatic):** the last step of every task is
  `/leadlens:audit --fix`. It re-reads the real diff, runs every gate
  (typecheck · lint · stylelint · tests · build), fixes all Blockers and Majors
  and re-audits, at most three loops.
- **Audit mode (on request):** "audit", "review" or "Lead Lens" plus a PR,
  branch, file or feature runs `/leadlens:audit <target>`. Report only, no
  edits unless told.
- **No evidence = UNVERIFIED, never PASS.**
- **Done = verdict SHIP or SHIP WITH NOTES, with the Lead Lens report in the
  final message.**

Modes, checklist, severities, verdict rules and report format live in the
plugin: `references/audit.md` under the LeadLens plugin root.

<!-- Task loop: make this the final step -->
8. **Run the Lead Lens** (`/leadlens:audit --fix`): self-review, simplify,
   verify, regression-test. Not done until the verdict is SHIP or SHIP WITH
   NOTES.

<!-- Task classifier rows -->
| **Styling / SCSS** | LeadLens `references/styling-tailwind-scss.md` | reuse tokens and mixins → implement → `/leadlens:audit --fix` |
| **Audit / PR review** | `/leadlens:audit <target>` | Lead Lens (Audit mode) → report |

<!-- Module index row -->
| `/leadlens:audit` | **Lead Lens**: evidence-based audit, severities, ship verdict |
